{templateType Trilobit\Core\Presentation\Styleguide\OverviewDefaultTemplate}

{*
 * Space, the axis of sizes controls and their icons share, and the widths a
 * layout is measured in - each drawn as long or as tall as it is, out of the
 * theme that is on. The list is FoundationTokens::SIZES.
 *}

{import '../../templates/furniture.latte'}

{block sgPage}
    <p class="l-measure">
        Space comes in steps rather than in lengths: a component asks for the room between the parts
        of one control, or between sections, and the theme decides how much that is. Controls share
        one axis of heights - a button, a field and a select of the same size line up in a row without
        a rule of their own - and the icon inside a control of each size is on the same axis.
    </p>

    <p class="l-measure">
        The widths of a window are numbers a media query has to write out, because a query cannot read
        a custom property; the tokens say which numbers those are. The widest bars below stop at the
        edge of their cell.
    </p>

    {foreach $sizeGroups as $heading => $group}
        {include sgTokenTable, heading: $heading, kind: $group['kind'], tokens: $group['tokens']}
    {/foreach}
{/block}
